WEBVTT

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:09.080
I shouldn't have gone on that spa trip!

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:11.620
It was fun,

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:12.950
but I'm an idiot!

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.920
Oh, it'll be fine!

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:16.820
It's just two days and one night anyway!

00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:19.160
You don't win a trip every day,

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.330
so I shouldn't let it go to waste.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:23.960
But doesn't Yanase have work, too?

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:26.180
He said he's fine.

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:29.460
You were supposed to be done with that
storyboard today. How's it coming along?

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:33.150
It's going really well right now,

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:36.470
so I can just finish it when I get back.

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:38.970
Yeah, right!

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:04.580
jounetsu tte kyuu ni wa michisuu sugiru

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:04.580
The concept of passion is full of so many unknowns

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:10.130
hanshateki hikiau youna tsuyoi jiryoku

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:10.130
A strong magnetic force is pulling us closer

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:14.760
risei no boudaarain karuku koete

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:14.760
Barely crossing the borderline of rationality

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:20.560
arawareta sono hi kara sorasenai

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:20.560
Ever since you appeared in my life, I can't turn away

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:25.560
itazura na unmei konsenchuu no kanjou ni

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:25.560
Whether it's my mischievous fate or conflicting emotions

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.400
rikutsu toka tsuuyou shin ai nda

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.400
Logic doesn't apply to them

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:33.780
te wo nobaseba wakaru

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:33.780
If I reach out my hand

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:36.150
hajimete no kimochi

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:36.150
Will you understand my feelings?

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:40.530
sekai ichi kimi ni koi wo shiteru

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:40.530
I'm in love with you, the greatest person in the world

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:44.910
ichibyou goto motto suki ni naru

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:44.910
I love you more and more every second

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:51.040
happi endo ni wa mada tooi

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:51.040
We're still far from a happy ending

00:01:51.170 --> 00:02:00.010
kanaetai yo futari dake no sutoorii

00:01:51.170 --> 00:02:00.010
But I want to make it come true

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.470
tsuzuite yuku

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.470
Our story continues

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:13.150
I bet Hatori's mad again.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:14.910
Mad? More like greasing the wheels at the printers.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:16.960
Just having to deal with the printer's again.

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:22.780
Waiting is an editor's job, so let him wait.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.470
Yanase's quite the philosopher.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:26.660
I am?

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:30.520
Which reminds me, you're pretty harsh with Tori.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:31.790
Not really.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:34.500
But they were...

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:38.300
So...

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:42.180
...is sarcasm the flip-side of affection?

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:44.680
Is he just embarrassed?

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:47.430
Oh, I see.

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:48.830
Wait.

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:54.440
Doesn't this mean I stole Yuu's guy?

00:02:58.860 --> 00:02:59.970
What?

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:02.290
I was thinking of taking a nap for an hour.

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:05.650
Oh, yeah, you've been up all night!

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:07.330
Yeah, of course! Go ahead!

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:14.510
So should I just go ahead and tell Tori?

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:15.300
No.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:16.460
That wouldn't be good either.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:20.060
It doesn't look like you're getting anything done!

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:23.260
Can you please stop slacking
off and keep drawing?

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:25.320
I'm not slacking off!

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:27.620
I was just thinking about the plot.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:28.970
The plot?

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:32.250
A, B, and C have this improbable relationship,

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:33.740
but really get along well.

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:35.850
A is in love with C,

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:38.240
and B is in love with A.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:42.190
C understands both of their positions,

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:44.250
but he really doesn't want
to be separated from A,

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:47.130
so he's thinking of confessing
his true feelings to A.

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:50.000
But what if B finds out?

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:52.850
Sounds heavy.

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:55.540
So would you make C the main character?

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:59.250
I don't know if readers can really
empathize with someone like that though.

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:01.850
These kinds of wishy-washy characters
are always so irritating.

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:03.730
Y-Yeah, I guess you're right.

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:06.570
And wanting to go out with A

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:09.410
while keeping B's friendship is just greedy.

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:13.400
I wouldn't want to see a girl
like that in one of your mangas.

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:17.650
Wait, could you be talking about yourself?

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:19.910
No, of course not!

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:21.770
So which one of them is you?

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:23.780
Oh my god, are you A?!

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:26.410
I told you, it's not me!

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:29.160
What's going on in here?

00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:32.390
I'm totally awake now.

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:34.160
Yanase, have you heard about this?

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:37.030
He's in some kind of a love conflict!

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:39.920
How many times do I have to tell
you, I was talking about the plot!

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:47.430
I hope he doesn't sense anything.

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:51.010
Whatever.

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:52.690
Before you start thinking up
plots for your new mangas,

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:54.490
maybe we should finish this one.

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:58.060
Sorry.

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:00.880
Good night!

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:02.320
We're leaving now!

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:04.100
Thanks a lot!

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:07.570
Thank god...

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:08.700
We're done.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.490
How about you take a bath or go to bed?

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:14.340
Yeah...

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:19.460
It's me. Let me in. I forgot the key.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:26.750
What's wrong with you?

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:29.470
I can't even move...

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:32.470
You haven't eaten yet, right?

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:35.770
I bet you haven't...

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:38.590
...eaten anything decent during crunch time.

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:55.160
Wow, he's got huge bags under his eyes.

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:57.620
It's ruining his good looks.

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:00.870
Is there something you want to say?

00:06:02.490 --> 00:06:07.080
Uh...no! Uh, everything went
okay with the manuscript, right?

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:09.970
I wouldn't be here if it hadn't.

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:11.460
I-I'm sorry.

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:14.640
Instead of apologizing, get your
stuff in before the deadline.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.190
Annoying.

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:21.130
Why are you still here?

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:22.620
Do you plan to eat here?

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:26.080
I'm going straight to my next job, so no.

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:28.170
And you over season the food when you cook.

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:29.660
No, that's the normal amount.

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:36.760
They're at it again.

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:43.300
Yuu loves him, so why can't he be honest?

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:47.850
So I heard you turned down the invitation...

00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:50.430
...for our company's New Year's party.

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:53.250
This time you've got to come.

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:55.980
They're putting your series on TV next year.

00:06:55.980 --> 00:06:57.570
You're the only author weird enough...

00:06:57.570 --> 00:07:00.390
...to not meet the people working on that project.

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:01.940
...But...

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:06.630
We'll make sure that nobody else finds
out that Chiharu Yoshikawa is a man,

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:07.740
so show up!

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:13.800
No way! I don't have anything appropriate
to wear, and I don't do those ritzy parties.

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:15.310
You should know that.

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:18.120
Anyway, I don't mind if they just turn
it into a TV show by themselves.

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:18.950
Ouch!

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:20.980
How old are you?!

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:22.830
That's not the issue.

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:27.710
I'll go if Yuu goes with me.

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:29.160
What?

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:33.530
It's not like you're going to be
around much that night anyway.

00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:35.980
Being alone will be boring.

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:37.590
Yuu, can you go?

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:39.350
Or are you already booked for work?

00:07:40.090 --> 00:07:43.390
No. All the other authors said they're going, too,

00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:44.480
so I'm free that day.

00:07:45.010 --> 00:07:46.620
Yes!

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:49.400
But I really don't have anything to wear.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:50.470
Well then...

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:52.280
I'll go shopping with you.

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:53.680
Really?

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:55.870
You've saved my life!

00:07:55.870 --> 00:08:00.530
I feel like I couldn't live without you.

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:05.500
Well, duh.

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:08.390
I'll call you when I'm done with work.

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:10.350
Sure! Good luck!

00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:14.600
Awesome!

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:26.240
Hey, Tori, what is that New Year's party like?

00:08:26.510 --> 00:08:28.530
Is it really full of celebrities?

00:08:28.910 --> 00:08:32.670
There will be actors and voice
actors involved with the adaptations,

00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:33.700
but it's mostly just authors.

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:35.240
Hmm, okay.

00:08:36.350 --> 00:08:37.740
You know,

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:41.380
I've never met any other manga authors,

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:43.750
so I'm kinda nervous about that.

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:47.250
Sheesh, what are you, a grade-schooler?

00:08:48.350 --> 00:08:51.300
You probably don't get it,

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:56.600
but if you always work alone,
being in a large crowd is intimidating.

00:08:57.220 --> 00:09:00.160
But I'm relieved that Yuu will be there.

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:02.110
That'll make it less daunting.

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:07.650
Wai...

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:21.040
S-Sorry...

00:09:24.970 --> 00:09:25.660
I'm going home.

00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:30.180
Home? What about the food?

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:33.730
Sorry for intruding. Get some rest tonight.

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:38.050
Wai-! Tori!

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:40.760
Tori!

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:50.060
It's not that easy to do pervy
things with your childhood friend.

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:55.110
He just kissed me without even thinking how I might feel.

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:02.080
And this thing...

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:05.090
What should I do about Yuu?

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:10.370
Yuu likes Tori, and Tori said he likes me...

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:13.570
But I like them both...

00:10:15.490 --> 00:10:18.260
I like Tori and Yuu, too.

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:20.090
But that feeling's...

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:25.720
But...

00:10:27.150 --> 00:10:30.350
Ahhh! No! No! No way in hell!

00:10:30.550 --> 00:10:32.080
Hm, wait...

00:10:33.510 --> 00:10:37.450
Does that mean Tori's special?

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:44.790
Wow!

00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:45.990
Marukawa Publishing would like
to continue working with you...

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:47.770
Marukawa Publishing New Year's Party

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:49.880
So everybody here is either a manga author,
or somehow involved in the process.

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:57.190
Yuu, have you been to a party like this before?

00:10:57.780 --> 00:10:59.680
Yeah, just once.

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:01.750
Wanna eat something?

00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:03.180
I'll go grab some stuff.

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:04.700
Yeah.

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:08.680
Yoshino.

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:10.690
Tori!

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:15.690
I bet you're going to ridicule my outfit.

00:11:16.220 --> 00:11:18.950
No, Yanase chose well.

00:11:18.950 --> 00:11:19.800
Huh?

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:21.570
Chief.

00:11:23.030 --> 00:11:24.830
Ah, Yoshino.

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:27.370
Hello.

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:29.660
This is our new editor.

00:11:30.280 --> 00:11:32.020
N-Nice to meet you.

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:33.210
My name is Ritsu Onodera.

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:34.840
Yoshino...

00:11:35.330 --> 00:11:37.530
Oh, that's my real last name.

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:39.210
My pen name is Chiharu Yoshikawa.

00:11:41.020 --> 00:11:42.720
Thank you for your work.

00:11:43.170 --> 00:11:46.290
Hatori, take care of the
introductions for the adaptation.

00:11:46.550 --> 00:11:47.220
Yes.

00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:49.520
I will see you later.

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:55.690
That's quite a young team member.

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:57.310
He's actually twenty-five,

00:11:57.720 --> 00:12:01.220
and he was in charge of Akihiko Usami at his old company.

00:12:01.560 --> 00:12:04.300
Usami? That novelist?

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:05.740
That's impressive.

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:09.620
The people involved with the adaptation are waiting, let's go.

00:12:09.930 --> 00:12:12.570
But Yuu's getting food right now.

00:12:12.570 --> 00:12:15.130
What's more important? It'll be over quickly.

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:22.130
We promise to turn this into a good product.

00:12:22.790 --> 00:12:24.640
We look forward to working with you.

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:28.140
Uh, well, I do, too...

00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:29.840
Excuse us.

00:12:37.700 --> 00:12:41.020
I knew this wasn't for me...

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:43.550
Oh, Tori-poo's there!

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:46.530
Tori-poo!

00:12:47.150 --> 00:12:49.380
Wait in the lobby when it's over.

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:50.960
We have to talk about the storyboard.

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:53.550
You want to have a meeting today, too?

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:55.520
There's no time until the deadline.

00:12:57.940 --> 00:13:01.050
Tori-poo, I'm not getting any hits at bingo.

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:04.240
And there's a huge line for the
sushi so you can't get any.

00:13:04.670 --> 00:13:08.160
Are you sure you don't want
to be an exclusive assistant?

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:09.050
I'm sorry.

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:11.030
I see.

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:14.330
My door is always open if you change your mind.

00:13:15.130 --> 00:13:16.720
Thank you very much.

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:19.480
Welcome back.

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:22.930
Sorry, I was meeting the adaptation people.

00:13:22.930 --> 00:13:25.620
Yeah, I saw Hatori took you over there.

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:27.800
Were you headhunted again?

00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:29.400
Yeah, but I turned it down.

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:30.300
Why?

00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:32.330
Wouldn't an exclusive position be more stable?

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:36.330
I wouldn't mind doing it for you.

00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:41.210
I'm honored, but I doubt you
could make a decent living with that.

00:13:41.470 --> 00:13:45.010
Yeah, that's why being freelance is fine for me.

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:49.720
Is that maybe...

00:13:50.540 --> 00:13:54.200
...because he can see Tori
when he comes to our studio?

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:55.790
Oh, it's Hatori.

00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:56.730
Huh?

00:13:58.110 --> 00:14:00.730
I think that's Erika Ichinose.

00:14:00.970 --> 00:14:03.090
Emerald's star author.

00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:06.240
So that's her...

00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:10.990
Anyway, he's been surrounded
by women this whole time.

00:14:12.070 --> 00:14:15.000
He seems to be enjoying
himself with his "work."

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:18.730
Tori's not in charge of her, is he?

00:14:19.150 --> 00:14:20.000
No idea.

00:14:20.410 --> 00:14:24.320
But I keep hearing that she's gunning for him.

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:25.510
Gunning for him?

00:14:25.970 --> 00:14:28.490
Inviting him to eat with her,

00:14:28.490 --> 00:14:30.240
dragging him into bars to discuss work...

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:32.510
Is that so...?

00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:35.140
I guess it's not that bad for him.

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:38.750
She might be older than him,

00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:40.690
but she's pretty and has money.

00:14:41.030 --> 00:14:42.770
Being a gold digger's not so bad.

00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:45.640
What's that supposed to mean?

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:51.180
It must be tough for you, too.

00:14:51.650 --> 00:14:54.910
I wonder why he's always so popular.

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:55.540
What?

00:14:56.180 --> 00:14:59.820
Remember how he was always
the one who was popular?

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:03.750
It might be the discrepancy
between his appearance,

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:05.920
and the fact that he's very caring.

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:08.300
So you think so, too...

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:09.240
Say what?

00:15:09.240 --> 00:15:10.810
Shit!

00:15:10.810 --> 00:15:14.560
Uh, so I guess that's why you like him, too?

00:15:15.230 --> 00:15:18.850
Please tell me why I have
to like someone like that?

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:19.940
Gross.

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:21.340
Huh?

00:15:21.340 --> 00:15:22.380
Sheesh.

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:25.970
You always make all these assumptions,

00:15:25.970 --> 00:15:27.440
and get these crazy ideas.

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:33.950
Oh, I was wrong. That's kind of a relief.

00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:37.120
Yea, I was shocked.

00:15:38.590 --> 00:15:40.080
I'm going home.

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:42.240
I'll go, too, then.

00:15:44.030 --> 00:15:45.820
Excuse me for a moment.

00:15:49.940 --> 00:15:50.720
Hey!

00:15:51.030 --> 00:15:53.250
Did you forget what I said?

00:15:54.350 --> 00:15:57.810
I didn't forget, but it looks like you're busy.

00:15:57.810 --> 00:15:59.270
Let's have our meeting tomorrow.

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:00.230
Hatori!

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:03.230
It looks like Ms. Ichinose is looking for you.

00:16:07.180 --> 00:16:07.980
See ya.

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:09.510
Hey!

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:28.880
Why did you go home?

00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:31.130
I told you we had a meeting.

00:16:31.460 --> 00:16:32.810
Are you serious?

00:16:32.810 --> 00:16:34.690
We have to do this when we have the time.

00:16:34.690 --> 00:16:36.810
Otherwise we'll have to go through
that mess again like last time.

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:39.890
This smell...

00:16:40.610 --> 00:16:43.710
That's totally somebody's perfume on him.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:46.020
Let's just get this over with.

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:48.520
That's supposed to be my line.

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:53.650
At this rate, there's not enough
monologue for the main character.

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:57.580
It's a bit of a stretch to get everything
across with just the expressions.

00:16:58.340 --> 00:16:59.660
And this right here...

00:17:00.150 --> 00:17:02.530
I guess it's not that bad for him.

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:05.540
This expression here...

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:07.750
Hey, are you listening?

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:09.100
I am.

00:17:09.100 --> 00:17:11.930
Say something if something is bugging you.

00:17:11.930 --> 00:17:13.760
I know!

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:16.630
You get it, don't you?

00:17:16.630 --> 00:17:20.560
You can't print something this boring
under Chiharu Yoshikawa's name.

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:22.930
Boring...

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:25.060
Fine!

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:27.060
I'll change it according to your wishes!

00:17:27.300 --> 00:17:29.350
What are you getting all upset about?

00:17:29.350 --> 00:17:31.420
I was just making suggestions.

00:17:31.420 --> 00:17:34.190
I'm tired and my brain's not working right.

00:17:34.510 --> 00:17:38.390
You're not the only one. What do you think work is?

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:43.080
I don't want to hear that from
someone who reeks of perfume!

00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:50.600
That woman was all over you the whole time,

00:17:50.600 --> 00:17:53.450
and you were all smiles for her! You must have had fun!

00:17:53.650 --> 00:17:55.250
That was work.

00:17:55.250 --> 00:17:57.250
I can't ignore a star author.

00:17:57.330 --> 00:18:00.310
Why are you reeking of perfume from working?!

00:18:00.310 --> 00:18:03.230
I guess the smell got on me
because I was around her.

00:18:03.230 --> 00:18:05.160
And why would you have to be so close...

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:06.810
...to her that her smell can rub off on you?!

00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:08.120
Yoshino!

00:18:09.610 --> 00:18:13.270
What the hell? It's like I'm jealous...

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:20.420
Aren't we going out?

00:18:20.760 --> 00:18:24.370
You never asked me or said anything!

00:18:24.940 --> 00:18:26.370
I think it was obvious!

00:18:26.660 --> 00:18:28.470
No, it wasn't!

00:18:28.470 --> 00:18:30.560
Besides, how am I supposed to know,

00:18:30.560 --> 00:18:32.860
when nothing's happened since then?!

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:35.510
I'm sorry.

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:41.650
Honestly, that's because I never
planned on saying anything, so...

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:48.890
Right now I don't know yet how to
adjust in and outside work...

00:18:56.290 --> 00:19:00.030
And wouldn't you be happier with Yanase?

00:19:01.190 --> 00:19:02.110
What?

00:19:02.110 --> 00:19:04.620
Be it the spa or the suit for the New Year's party,

00:19:05.050 --> 00:19:07.760
you always ask him first.

00:19:09.820 --> 00:19:13.040
That was because I thought you'd be too busy!

00:19:13.470 --> 00:19:14.800
I know that,

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:17.330
but there are things that I
can't just rationalize away.

00:19:19.290 --> 00:19:22.050
On top of that, last time you pushed me away...

00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:28.810
Th-That was because you kind of forced me!

00:19:29.530 --> 00:19:33.810
I think it's normal to be confused
when you suddenly do something like that.

00:19:34.130 --> 00:19:37.940
Anyway, why are you making Yuu your enemy?

00:19:38.390 --> 00:19:43.070
I don't want to ever kiss or be
kissed by any man except for you!

00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:50.330
Why do I have to say something like this?!

00:19:50.940 --> 00:19:52.990
So it's okay if it's not sudden?

00:19:54.570 --> 00:19:55.590
P-Probably...

00:19:56.350 --> 00:19:59.090
So is now okay?

00:19:59.710 --> 00:20:01.700
R-Right now?

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:06.600
All right...

00:20:14.260 --> 00:20:16.650
If you say you need it spelled out,

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:18.280
I'll say it as many times as you want.

00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:20.860
I love you.

00:20:21.270 --> 00:20:23.110
It has to be you.

00:20:23.790 --> 00:20:25.120
Are you daft?

00:20:25.120 --> 00:20:26.420
Usually you're so quiet,

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:29.790
but now you're calmly spitting out
these really embarrassing lines!

00:20:32.020 --> 00:20:33.160
Your answer?

00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:35.250
I'll do my best.

00:20:59.550 --> 00:21:01.900
You do over season the food.

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:04.410
It's not like I'm making the food for you.

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:07.500
Too much sodium will lead to high blood pressure.

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:09.220
That's none of your business anyway.

00:21:10.930 --> 00:21:14.160
Oh, yeah, during that New Year's
party Chiaki was suddenly like,

00:21:14.490 --> 00:21:17.540
"You like Tori, too, right?"

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:18.730
That was a surprise.

00:21:18.730 --> 00:21:19.920
Hey, Yuu!

00:21:20.280 --> 00:21:21.460
What?

00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:24.570
Chiaki's look was so earnest.

00:21:24.570 --> 00:21:25.680
That was just-!

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:30.180
Anyway, if you don't, is there
someone else you like?!

00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:32.430
Yeah, there is.

00:21:34.070 --> 00:21:35.440
What?!

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:38.440
Who is it? Who? Is it someone I know?!

00:21:38.790 --> 00:21:40.940
I think Hatori knows that someone quite well.

00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:45.140
What? Tori, you know!? Who is it?

00:21:45.140 --> 00:21:46.710
Just finish eating and get to work.

00:21:46.710 --> 00:21:49.580
Hey, tell me!

